       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/c5db0a47d1b953fb365572bcefb156ed?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSP-3.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/c5db0a47d1b953fb365572bcefb156ed?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSP-3.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/c5db0a47d1b953fb365572bcefb156ed?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSP-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Scott Prater",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A75d3a172-f88d-4ef1-85ad-1c4a45ad0f97",
      "timeZone": "America/Chicago"
     },
     "body": "<p>I'm seeing the same two errors in fcrepo-common when building Fedora 3.4RC1 in Eclipse (3.6, Helios) with the Maven m2eclipse plugin.  Any way to manually fix this in the short term, perhaps from the command line?</p>\n\n<p>Edit:  Using Chris Wilper's instructions on <a href=\"https://wiki.duraspace.org/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=13765655#HowdoyouconfigureEclipseforFedorawithMaven%3F-updatemvn\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://wiki.duraspace.org/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=13765655#HowdoyouconfigureEclipseforFedorawithMaven%3F-updatemvn</a> (first comment), I was able to get a clean build.  I needed to run \"Maven -&gt; Update Project Configuration\" in Eclipse on fcrepo-client-repo after importing the prebuilt source. </p>",
     "created": "06/Aug/10 1:28 AM",
     "id": "11500",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10489/comment/11500",
